Common Signs Your AC Needs Repair
Many homeowners overlook early warning signs until the system completely stops working. Watch for these common indicators:

Warm Air Coming from Vents
If your air conditioner is blowing warm or weak airflow, it may have refrigerant problems, clogged filters, or compressor issues.

Strange Noises
Grinding, rattling, buzzing, or squealing sounds often indicate loose parts, worn bearings, or motor problems that require immediate attention.

High Energy Bills
An unexpected increase in utility costs usually means your AC system is working harder than necessary due to hidden mechanical issues.

Frequent Cycling
If your air conditioner constantly turns on and off, it may have thermostat problems or airflow restrictions.
Water Leaks
Moisture around your indoor unit can indicate a clogged condensate drain or frozen evaporator coil.
